{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-openplanner-5-graph-connections-1793664019642", :event/time "2026-11-03T00:00:19.642Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "openplanner-5-graph-connections", :dependency [], :parent "openplanner-system-projections-rest-compat", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793664019641-0.csvy8gwm58gcs2douvx", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Repair graph connection projection", :source-path "/home/err/Documents/Codex/2026-11-02/task-23/openplanner5-local-repair/kanban/repair-graph-connection-projection-nections.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Repair graph connections and textless event projection\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe served graph and event APIs preserve induced edges at the node cap, attribute Bluesky mentions through observed authorship, and project predecessor, topic and attachment edges for textless Discord events.\n\n## Scope\n\nDestination: Clojure-family graph/event projection and an explicitly verified HTTP and Mongo boundary, under the system projections and REST compatibility epic.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nChanging identity claims, historical backfill, ordering guarantees, authentication or production data.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The existing real-HTTP/disposable-Mongo characterization passes all seven checks, including cap-boundary, authorship and all three textless edges.\n- Every existing route and write behavior exposed by the replaced or adapted TypeScript implementation is characterized and retained.\n- Named external adapters normalize foreign values to Clojure data and real service integration is tested separately from stubs.\n- No new TypeScript implementation is introduced; existing TypeScript remains intact unless its replacement is fully characterized.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun the existing ClojureScript characterization with disposable MongoDB and loopback HTTP, targeted and integrated tests, lint, and independent review. Record Kafka/Clio and migration limitations."}, :causal/root "55f7baf2-2e39-4d02-bcb3-01790ca25850"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-openplanner-5-detached-vector-failures-1793678392641", :event/time "2026-11-03T03:59:52.641Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "openplanner-5-detached-vector-failures", :dependency [], :parent "openplanner-5-graph-connections", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1793678392640-0.35j42r1u9noydz4kr57", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Investigate detached event vector write failures", :source-path "/home/err/Documents/Codex/2026-11-02/task-23/openplanner5-local-repair/kanban/investigate-detached-event-vector-write-failures-failures.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Investigate detached event-vector write failures\n\n## Outcome\n\nIdentify and correct the inherited Mongo write failures observed in detached event-vector and graph-node embedding work, with an explicit, verified account of response and failure behavior. This task follows `openplanner-5-graph-connections`; the five graph/textless examples do not resolve these failures.\n\n## Evidence\n\nIn isolated reference and candidate replica-set tests involving non-string event IDs, both HTTP routes returned 200 while three hot-vector writes failed because an `_id` value was an array and two graph-node embedding writes failed with duplicate-key errors. The instrumented runs recorded five terminal warnings in each route. One reference run also recorded a retryable WiredTiger write-conflict attempt; its ultimate outcome was not established. Synthetic embeddings and disabled Kafka were used. The bounded observation window does not prove that no later or uninstrumented work exists.\n\n## Scope and acceptance\n\n- Reproduce each failure against unchanged reference behavior using disposable Mongo and Clojure-family tests, preserving exact input, stored records, response counters, logs and failure timing.\n- Identify event-ID and graph-embedding key/uniqueness semantics and demonstrate a safe, idempotent persistence strategy for supported input shapes without losing data or changing status/error behavior implicitly.\n- Verify actual persisted vector/embedding records, duplicate and collision handling, transient write-failure handling, and shutdown/task settlement; explicitly distinguish retry attempts from eventual outcomes.\n- Characterize Kafka, real embedding-provider and cross-service behavior separately; do not infer it from synthetic providers.\n- Record any required public API or data-migration decision before changing existing contracts. New OpenPlanner implementation and tests use Clojure-family code with named foreign-value adapters.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nBackfilling production data, changing credentials or security settings, production deployment, or hiding detached failures behind successful assertion counts."}, :causal/root "35cada22-699e-4877-aeb7-b05e78ad534e"}
